External correctness corpora (conformance/logic/cases/external/)
  These are reasoning correctness test corpora — NOT part of the published CC BY 4.0
  GMEOW vocabulary. Each corpus carries a corpus.json declaring its SPDX license; only
  IMPORT_OK-licensed corpora are vendored here (enforced by the native license policy
  in crates/conformance/src/license.rs). Restrictive/unknown-licensed suites are never
  committed — they may only be fetched live in the non-required Lane-B lane.
  - szs-mini, w3c-mini — self-authored by Blackcat Informatics® Inc., CC BY 4.0.
    Tiny seed corpora establishing the external-corpus convention.
  - tptp-mini, tptp-mini-divergence — self-authored by Blackcat Informatics® Inc.,
    CC BY 4.0, in TPTP FOF/CNF syntax (the format defined at https://www.tptp.org/).
    The FOL problem bodies are parsed for real, reduced by the FOL-negation
    refutation, and lowered onto the native DL consistency engine. The agreeing
    Lane-A subset (tptp-mini) is decided in agreement with each problem's SZS
    status; the source-only tptp-mini-divergence lane holds genuine first-order
    problems the native EL/DL fragment cannot decide, pinned as honest capability
    gaps. No third-party TPTP distribution problems are vendored — those are
    fetched live only in the non-required Lane-B lane, audited per problem.
  - ontouml-mini, ontouml-mini-divergence — self-authored by Blackcat Informatics®
    Inc., CC BY 4.0, in the OntoUML metamodel vocabulary (https://w3id.org/ontouml#,
    the serialization the FAIR OntoUML/UFO model catalog uses). Each model is parsed
    for real and lowered onto the native world-scoped logic: stereotype ABox, then
    graded by the five native OntoUML foundation disciplines; the fired discipline
    set is compared to the model's documented anti-pattern verdict (the community's
    anti-pattern catalogue, https://ontouml.readthedocs.io/en/latest/anti-patterns/).
    The agreeing Lane-A subset (ontouml-mini) reproduces each documented verdict and
    keeps clean controls violation-free; the source-only ontouml-mini-divergence lane
    holds documented anti-patterns the native fragment cannot reproduce — a capability
    gap (an out-of-fragment stereotype) or a coverage gap (a documented pattern no
    native discipline decides) — pinned as honest gaps. The real FAIR OntoUML/UFO
    catalog (github.com/OntoUML/ontouml-models) is CC BY-SA 4.0 (ReferenceOnly under
    the native license policy) and is NEVER committed; it is graded live only in the
    non-required Lane-B lane, each model's own license audited.
  - entailment-mini, entailment-mini-divergence — self-authored by Blackcat
    Informatics® Inc., CC BY 4.0, a set of W3C OWL test-ontology-style entailment
    tests (PositiveEntailmentTest / NegativeEntailmentTest) carrying BOTH an inline
    RDF/XML premise and an inline RDF/XML conclusion. Each is graded by the native
    entailment-by-refutation reduction (A ⊨ C iff premise ∪ ¬C is inconsistent) over
    the DL consistency engine. The agreeing Lane-A subset (entailment-mini) is graded
    with a real native verdict agreeing with the declared outcome; the
    entailment-mini-divergence lane holds conclusions outside the soundly-refutable
    single-EDB fragment (a multi-triple conjunction, or a role assertion whose
    negation is not EL-expressible) pinned as honest, structured capability gaps. No
    third-party test-suite documents are vendored here; the upstream W3C entailment
    suites express premise/conclusion as reference documents graded live only in the
    non-required Lane-B lane.
  - w3c-owl2-el — W3C OWL 2 conformance test cases (ConsistencyTest /
    InconsistencyTest, OWL 2 EL profile subset). Original suite maintained by
    the W3C OWL Working Group and archived at:
      https://www.w3.org/2009/11/owl-test/
    Copyright 2009 W3C (Massachusetts Institute of Technology, ERCIM, Keio,
    Beihang). Licensed under the W3C Software and Document License. A curated
    Lane-A subset of 12 cases (those decidable by the native EL reasoner) is
    vendored under conformance/logic/cases/external/w3c-owl2-el/.
  - ORE 2015 Reasoner Competition Corpus — NOT vendored, fetched live only.
    Zenodo DOI 10.5281/zenodo.18578 (Matentzoglu & Parsia, University of
    Manchester). The corpus is licensed for reasoner-BENCHMARKING use ONLY and
    NOT for redistribution: "the open access extends only to this purpose; all
    individual ontologies retain their own license restrictions; removal on
    request". So NO ORE ontology is committed to this repository. The
    `make maint-external-corpora` Lane-B lane DOWNLOADS a bounded subset to a
    gitignored scratch dir for benchmarking use (license-compliant) and grades
    the native reasoner against it for consistency soundness; the per-ontology
    divergences are written as a gmeow:Finding graph and never folded into the
    committed bundle.

Vendored corpora (crates/lang-bridge/tests/vendored/)
  Ring-fenced, fully-attributed third-party corpus fragments used only as native
  correctness fixtures — NOT part of the published CC BY 4.0 GMEOW vocabulary and
  never merged into it. Each fragment carries a corpus.json declaring its SPDX
  license, source URL, upstream ref, attribution, and ring-fence flag; only a
  ring-fenced + fully-attributed CC BY-SA fragment clears vendoring (enforced by
  gmeow_license::policy_for_vendored_corpus).
  - UD_English-EWT (en_ewt-ud-dev-fragment.conllu) — a three-sentence fragment of
    the Universal Dependencies English Web Treebank (UD_English-EWT), reproduced
    verbatim. Copyright the Universal Dependencies project and the EWT treebank
    authors, licensed CC BY-SA 4.0. Source:
      https://raw.githubusercontent.com/UniversalDependencies/UD_English-EWT/b7711cce01cdd4f5fcc0a8199b8a50d951b16c0c/en_ewt-ud-dev.conllu
    Upstream ref: release r2.18 (commit b7711cce01cdd4f5fcc0a8199b8a50d951b16c0c).
    The fragment exercises the lang: CoNLL-U byte round-trip
    (Gate 2); the exact sentences vendored are declared by sent_id in its
    corpus.json.
